Z||000009||artherd||11-16-2001||12:04 AM||||Whups, thought you had an 88 for some reason... (look at the screen name, dummy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>84-87s are more of a pain, but not impossible...   I still think that shop is being a bit lazy (well, depends, if they're $49.95 cut-rate prices to begin with, then they'll loose money on a Fiero.  But for a hundred bucks or so, to any decent and non-BSing shop you should be able to get it aligned.<P>Look *carefully* at your car after they are done, make sure they don't bung up anything.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>PS: the tape measure is only to get your car the few miles to a shop, don't try to drive like that for any legenth of time!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I have been able to reliably get within a few tenths of a degree of spec. though.   88s are scary-easy to align!<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000010||tgowens||11-16-2001||02:53 AM||||I replace shocks and struts all the time on Fieros and when replacing the strut I snug the two 24mm bolts through the strut and the knuckle, then pull out on the bottom of the knuckle while pushing in at the bolt location  then tightening the two bolts - this sets it close enough that the alignment shop has minimal trouble setting the alignment. Have sent 84's through 88's to the same alignment shop and haven't had a problem under normal circumstances.<P>Abnormal circumstances have been where a knuckle has been bent due to a sideways curbing or other accident......<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Spektrum-87GT||11-16-2001||07:50 PM||||sideways curbing is what happened!!<BR>labor came out to 130 for the alignment... a bit more than usual, but this wasnt the norm. I'm very pleased with the job they did too.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by tgowens:<BR><B>I replace shocks and struts all the time on Fieros and when replacing the strut I snug the two 24mm bolts through the strut and the knuckle, then pull out on the bottom of the knuckle while pushing in at the bolt location  then tightening the two bolts - this sets it close enough that the alignment shop has minimal trouble setting the alignment. Have sent 84's through 88's to the same alignment shop and haven't had a problem under normal circumstances.<P>Abnormal circumstances have been where a knuckle has been bent due to a sideways curbing or other accident......<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||artherd||11-17-2001||01:01 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by tgowens:<BR><B><BR>Abnormal circumstances have been where a knuckle has been bent due to a sideways curbing or other accident......<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Heh.   Fiero Shop is Richmond, CA. is great  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>(Long story, but a curb jumped out in front of my car, and bent both the rear knuckle, and cradle. I swapped both; and everything else; out, looking for what was bent. but didn't swap knuckles and cradles at the same time.)  Man, that 88 *rear* knuckle is beefy! (but it was bent, day before a show Terry and George saved my butt  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Thanks guys!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
